## Recommended Next Steps

Formalize the general Bayes-gap lemma as the reusable finite-horizon lower-bound atom.

Keep the q-scaled construction as evidence that \(qD\) valuable delayed tail mass can force \(qD\) regret under unknown-class quantifiers.

For rate matching, try a different construction: repeated blocks with limited information leakage, or a two-point statistical lower bound where terminal observations have small KL/TV but the optimal quotes remain separated. The current q-scaled atom alone is not enough for matching power-tail lower rates.
