+
 Technical hygiene for future statements: use \(\sup_a\) instead of \(\max_a\) unless attainment is proved; state whether prices are exogenous or action-dependent; state whether the learner knows the law or must be uniform over an unknown class; state whether algorithms may depend on the horizon \(T\). The known-law oracle lemma is horizon-aware and does not settle anytime, computational, unknown-law, or action-dependent models.
